  "kanji": "官",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 官\ntitle: government official\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 宀\nradicalNumber: 40\nonyomi: [カン]\nkunyomi: []\ndistractors: [客, 同, 富]\n---\n\n# 官 — government official\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 宀 (no. 40) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n官 marks an official or government connection in words such as [警官](../words/警官.md) (けいかん), \"police officer,\" and 官庁 (かんちょう), \"government office.\"\nIt also has an organ sense in 器官 (きかん), so an official is not the only possible meaning.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the stacked boxlike forms under 宀 as an official's filing trays.\nThis office scene is a memory aid, not a historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カン | on | [警官](../words/警官.md) (けいかん) — police officer; 官庁 (かんちょう) — government office |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [警官](../words/警官.md) (けいかん) — police officer\n- 官庁 (かんちょう) — government office; agency\n- 器官 (きかん) — organ of a living body\n\n## Notes\n\nInspect the connected lower outline rather than remembering only \"roof plus boxes.\"\n[客](客.md) and [富](富.md) have different material beneath the roof; [同](同.md) has an outer enclosure rather than 宀.\nThe biology word 器官 is a separate lexical use, not a claim that a body organ is a government official.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project); [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1252330, 1211730, 1218910.\n",
